"Adaptive Text" by "Tester"

[I7-lite 7c: adaptive text with a fixed viewpoint - the player is 'you',
 present tense. Verbs agree with the object named most recently.]

To reach is a verb. To carry is a verb. To look is a verb. To flow is a verb.

The Stream Bank is a room. "[We] [are] standing beside a stream. [We] [have] a feeling [we] [are] not alone [here]."
The brook is scenery in the Stream Bank. The description of the brook is "[The brook] [flow] out of the building."
The set of keys is in the Stream Bank. The keys are plural-named. The indefinite article of the keys is "some".
The lamp is in the Stream Bank.

Instead of examining the keys, say "[regarding the keys][They] [are] shiny, and [they] [reach] the floor."
Instead of examining the lamp, say "[The lamp] [are] dull. [They] [carry] a dent."
Instead of examining yourself, say "[We] [look] fine. [Our] cloak is wet."
Instead of waiting, say "[regarding the lamp][There] [are] nothing to do [now]."
